# Exp41 — Shared Discrete-Time Competing-Risk Survival Law — FROZEN / EXECUTION ISSUED

Date frozen: 2026-08-13, after Exp40 completion and before any Exp41 fit or score.

Scientific question: can ONE shared TRAIN-fitted discrete-time competing-risk law generate coherent 15/30/60/120m cumulative probabilities using only starting `CorridorPosition` and `Dwell`, instead of fitting separate Position/Dwell coefficients by horizon?

Frozen universe:
- exact backbone above must reproduce;
- cutoff `< 2026-08-13 00:00:00 BRT`;
- same TRAIN / Validation / exploratory TEST splits;
- fixed starting ACTIVE L1-L2 boundaries;
- future path uses M5 CLOSE only;
- at-risk steps `k=1..24`;
- first ADV/REC close crossing terminates risk;
- gap/split/end-of-data censors if reached first;
- starting covariates are frozen `geo0=logit(CorridorPosition)` and `dwell0=log1p(DwellBars)`.

Frozen shared hazard laws:

```text
BASE_SURV:
  ADV vs STAY = alpha_ADV[k]
  REC vs STAY = alpha_REC[k]

POSITION_SURV:
  ADV vs STAY = alpha_ADV[k] + beta_ADV_geo * geo0
  REC vs STAY = alpha_REC[k] + beta_REC_geo * geo0

SEMI_SURV:
  ADV vs STAY = alpha_ADV[k] + beta_ADV_geo * geo0 + beta_ADV_dwell * dwell0
  REC vs STAY = alpha_REC[k] + beta_REC_geo * geo0 + beta_REC_dwell * dwell0
```

There are 24 elapsed-step nuisance intercepts per cause. Position/Dwell coefficients are shared across all 24 future steps; no elapsed-time interaction is allowed.

Recursive cumulative output:

```text
S(H)       = P(NO_EXIT through H)
CIF_ADV(H) = P(ADVANCE first by H)
CIF_REC(H) = P(RECAPTURE first by H)
```

for exactly `15/30/60/120m`.

Primary estimand: same eligible Exp40 `state x horizon` cells, pooled `STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED`, whole-BRT-day bootstrap.

Formal gates:

```text
Gate A: POSITION_SURV vs BASE_SURV
Gate B: SEMI_SURV vs POSITION_SURV

SHARED_SURVIVAL_POSITION_CORE = PASS only if Gate A passes Brier+LL in VAL+TEST
SHARED_SURVIVAL_DWELL_INCREMENT = PASS only if Gate B passes Brier+LL in VAL+TEST
SHARED_SURVIVAL_CORRIDOR_LAW = PASS only if both pass
```

Coverage below 70% in any split => `UNDERPOWERED_COVERAGE`.

Diagnostics only:
- shared beta coefficients;
- 24 step-specific baseline hazards;
- horizon point gains;
- EXIT/SIDE AUC;
- exact cumulative monotonicity/coherence;
- descriptive price of sharing versus the Exp40 horizon-specific `SEMI_H`.

Anti-rescue:

```text
NO horizon-specific geo/dwell coefficients after result
NO elapsed-time interaction with geo/dwell
NO alternative step bins/splines/polynomials
NO horizon additions/removals
NO Position/Dwell thresholds or buckets
NO Exp38/Exp39 coordinates
NO D1/Clock/Z/Fib/weekday/Scale/Energy/HMM interaction
NO Validation/TEST refit
NO Exp27 scoring/modification
```

If Exp41 fails while Exp40 remains strong, interpretation is: Position+Dwell has multi-horizon predictive depth, but this simple proportional shared discrete-time law is insufficient. Exp40 remains valid.

Execution contract issued in the research chat after this freeze:
- exact Exp20/21 guards;
- exact Exp40 eligible-cell guards by split and horizon;
- person-period TRAIN likelihood with one row per observed future 5m at-risk interval;
- numerical-only Hessian stabilization `1e-10`;
- no scientific parameter or target change;
- no Exp41 score inspected before issuing the implementation.

Historical OOS remains exploratory. Runtime promotion = NONE.
